  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3aa88570-b387-4df3-8038-927062b23e46-image.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 195px;\" /><br /><br />To find point of intersection of given chord <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></math> with the given circle <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> eliminate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;from two equations<br />Point of intersection&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the corresponding ordinates.<br />Point of intersection&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br />Diametric form of equation of circle,<br /><math><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> .</p>",
